@SYSTEM_TITLE
PRINTL before
; An island is an overlay held off the log: the markup builds its own lines,
; which the front-end draws over the console, so nothing an island prints ever
; joins the line flow — not the printed text, not LINECOUNT. The markup is
; parsed in full, so a script still sees Emuera's tag diagnostics.
HTML_PRINT_ISLAND "<div width='40' height='2'>island</div>"
HTML_PRINT_ISLAND "plain", 2
; A second print to a layer stacks on it instead of replacing it.
HTML_PRINT_ISLAND "<div ypos='-100'>over</div>", 2
PRINTFORML lines {LINECOUNT}
; One layer, then every layer.
HTML_PRINT_ISLAND_CLEAR 2
HTML_PRINT_ISLAND_CLEAR
PRINTL after
; ...and a normal HTML_PRINT still prints, so nothing about the island path
; leaks into the console.
HTML_PRINT "<b>bold</b>"
